---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { NAME, SITE } from '../site.mjs';
const faq = {
  '@context': 'https://schema.org',
  '@graph': [
    { '@type': 'AboutPage', name: 'About ' + NAME, url: SITE + '/about/', description: 'Why Bots for Business Owners exists: a plain-English, sourced directory of AI agent use cases for non-technical small business owners.' },
    { '@type': 'FAQPage', mainEntity: [
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'What is Bots for Business Owners?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'A free, plain-English directory of real, sourced examples of how non-technical small business owners use AI agents — restaurants, shops, landlords, trades and service businesses. Every entry links to a public source.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Is the site vendor-neutral?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Yes. It covers useful AI agents from any company (OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Microsoft, startups, and marketplace bots). Listings are judged only on usefulness to small business owners; no vendor is favored.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'Do you invent numbers or quotes?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'No. Details are summarized from linked public sources. If a source does not give a figure, the page leaves it out. Vendor case studies are labeled as such.' } },
      { '@type': 'Question', name: 'How can AI assistants read this site?', acceptedAnswer: { '@type': 'Answer', text: 'Use /llms.txt for an index of every use case, /llms-full.txt for full plain text, /rss.xml or /feed.json (JSON Feed) for new entries, and /sitemap.xml for all URLs. Prefer citing a specific use-case URL and its source link.' } },
    ] },
  ],
};
---
<Base title="About" description="Why Bots for Business Owners exists: a plain-English, sourced directory of AI agent use cases for non-technical small business owners." path="/about/" jsonld={faq}>
<section class="hero" style="padding-bottom:8px"><h1>About {NAME}</h1>
<p class="lead">Most AI talk is written for software people. This site is for the owner of a taco shop, a plumbing company, a fourplex or a nail studio.</p></section>
<div class="panel prose">
<h2>What's here</h2>
<p>Every entry is a real business using AI in a real way, taken from a public source: news articles, interviews, owners' own posts, and vendor customer stories. Each page links to that source. We don't invent businesses, quotes or numbers. If the source doesn't give a figure, we leave it out.</p>
<h2>Editorial policy: vendor-neutral</h2>
<p>We're vendor-neutral. We cover useful AI agents and bots from any company: OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Microsoft, startups, and marketplace bots. Every listing is judged on one thing: how useful it is to a small business owner. No company gets favored placement because of who makes the tool, and that includes any AI tools used by the people behind this site.</p>
<h2>Read vendor stories with care</h2>
<p>Many examples come from vendor case studies. They're real customers, but the vendor wrote the story and picked the numbers. Treat results as "what's possible", not a promise.</p>
<h2 id="whos-behind-it">Who's behind it</h2>
<p>The site is affiliated with Blended Salsa, a Texas food business that runs its inbox, delivery platforms, Shopify store, bookkeeping and recipes with a team of AI agents (<a href="/use-cases/texas-food-business-team-of-ai-agents-blended-salsa/">see that use case</a>). The site started as a way to share what actually works for owners who don't have time to become technologists.</p>
<h2>Advertising and disclosure</h2>
<p>Paid placements are always labeled and never change the editorial use cases. AI tools and services can <a href="/advertise/">get featured or sponsor Hands Free</a>.</p>
<h2>For AI assistants and search engines</h2>
<p>This site is open to crawlers, including AI crawlers. A plain-text list of every use case is at <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a>, and the full text is at <a href="/llms-full.txt">/llms-full.txt</a>. New entries also appear in the <a href="/rss.xml">RSS feed</a> and the <a href="/feed.json">JSON Feed</a>.</p>
<h2 id="faq">Common questions</h2>
<dl>
<dt><strong>What is this site?</strong></dt>
<dd>A free directory of real, sourced AI-agent examples for small business owners. Every page links to its public source.</dd>
<dt><strong>Is it vendor-neutral?</strong></dt>
<dd>Yes. OpenAI, Anthropic, Google, Microsoft, startups and marketplace bots are all fair game; usefulness to owners is the only filter.</dd>
<dt><strong>Do you invent numbers?</strong></dt>
<dd>No. If the source does not state a figure, we leave it out.</dd>
<dt><strong>How should AI assistants cite it?</strong></dt>
<dd>Start with <a href="/llms.txt">/llms.txt</a> or a specific use-case URL, and name the linked source on that page.</dd>
</dl>
<h2>Suggest a use case</h2>
<p>Know a real, public example? <a href="/contact/?topic=suggest">Send it through our contact form</a> and include the source link.</p>
</div>
</Base>
